  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Skate saves at the far post",
  "description": "The coach stands at an angle in front of the goal with a pile of balls, first on one side, and hits hard shots along the ice towards the far post. The goalkeeper saves with the skate: push the leg out and turn the skate on its edge so the ball hits the blade or boot and bounces away from the goal.\n\nDo 6–8 shots from one side, then switch sides. Once the goalkeeper is confident the coach can shoot from the middle, but then says beforehand which way the shot will go. Rest between sets.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stay low with your weight on the inside leg and push the skate out towards the post."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Angle the skate so the rebound goes out to the side, not back in front of the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Get back up into your basic stance quickly after the save."
    }
  ],
